  "section_title": "5. Research design and transparency",
  "block_count": 10,
  "scope_snapshot": [
    {
      "type": "p",
      "html": "The original conditional-study design and selected parameters were publicly frozen before their respective executions. The FX evaluation interval had already been inspected. Subsequent inference, AR replay, rank and preference analyses, parsimonious regression, maximal-inequality simulations, aggregate-panel extension and mature-baseline additions are post-result / exploratory. Local execution bindings do not create a new public preregistration. A dagger (†) marks these analyses in tables and figure captions; it applies throughout the Supplement, with the section-wide post-result label in S16 also covering its unmarked tables. Equal-loss tests are working-reference diagnostics under their stated dependence and moment assumptions, not selection-adjusted confirmation. The full retrospective record and unsuccessful cells remain visible.",
