    {
      "type": "p",
      "html": "A deliberately invalid H6 label-timing control retains the original selected parameters, long history and refit clock on predetermined first, middle and last complete blocks: 72 FX origins and 39 Treasury origins. Replacing the clean pool ending at r−H with one ending at r includes 6 immature labels per refit. In Treasury QR the illegal oracle reduces loss by 33.3988% but changes breaches from 5 to 6; FX QR instead raises loss by 0.0639%. The complete QR, KNN and F outcomes in Supplement Table S37 have mixed directions. This post-result / exploratory control quantifies timing contamination in these blocks, not an inevitable optimism bias or an all-sample performance effect.",
