    {
      "type": "p",
      "html": "The stipulated pinball score weights an underprediction dollar nineteen times an overprediction dollar. It is a consistent quantile score (Gneiting, 2011), rather than an observed financial cost. We report U=mean(P−C)<sub>+</sub>, the mean underprediction amount, and V=mean(C−P)<sub>+</sub>, the mean overprediction amount. Both average over all forecast origins; conditional breach severity averages over each method's own strict P&gt;C event set. The reported headroom C−B is distinct from V. Archived fields mean_positive_overrun, mean_unused_allowance and mean_extra_allowance correspond to U, V and mean(C−B); their historical names do not represent resources actually allocated. Lower mean loss and fewer breach occasions are separate outcomes. Financial units are never pooled across sources.",
      "_generator": "v6:block:manuscript:4:6",
