    {
      "type": "p",
      "html": "Kupiec (1995) proportion-of-failures and Christoffersen (1998) independence/conditional-coverage diagnostics use the original first-origin-plus-j(H+1) grid. Conditional coverage here adds full-sample-grid POF to the transition-independence LR. A DQ-type full-sample HAC Wald adaptation of Engle and Manganelli (2004) uses the intercept, issue-known capacity and matured hit lags H+1 through H+4. Singular covariance or an unidentified transition row yields NA. The fixed 72-member common-history equal-loss ranking family receives Holm (1979) adjustment; exact identical losses use conservative p=1 solely for multiplicity bookkeeping. Supplement S9 and the output CSVs retain all statistics and statuses. The additional benchmarks in Supplement S16 use a separately stated transition-conditional CC likelihood on adjacent sparse-grid pairs, conditioning on the initial hit; their values do not replace this archived convention. Their ranking families are frozen separately, and NA adjustment bookkeeping is kept distinct from an observed p-value.",
